  "description": "You're Nike, and you want to own the whole shoe game.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Nike, Inc.: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nike,_Inc.\n\nFrom the cited page: founded January 25, 1964, as Blue Ribbon Sports by Bill Bowerman and Phil Knight, first distributing Onitsuka Tiger shoes from Japan; in 1971 Bowerman used his wife's waffle iron to experiment with rubber soles; the company officially became Nike, Inc. on May 30, 1971, and first used the Swoosh, designed by Carolyn Davidson, on June 18, 1971; it went public in December 1980; it signed Michael Jordan in 1984, which led to the Air Jordan brand; the \"Just Do It\" slogan debuted July 1, 1988; it bought Converse in 2003 for $309 million; fiscal 2025 revenue was $46.3 billion. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #nike #airjordan #howtheymakemoney",
